{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1275149-christian-orthodox-euthanatoi","id":1275149,"title":"Christian Orthodox Euthanatoi?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-12-18T12:55:03-08:00","id":1275149,"title":"Christian Orthodox Euthanatoi?","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\">Yo - I've recently stumbled upon this White Wolf Wiki paragraph on the Euthanatoi, and it has triggered my curiosity, as I am seeking to create a character meant to be placed in the Eastern European part of the world, around Bulgaria, Romania, Ukraine, something of the sorts, where people mostly practice Christianism. <br /> <br /> White Wolf Wiki on Euthanatos: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Mantras can only be passed on orally; written mantras are &quot;dead&quot; and supposedly have no power. Some Euthanatoi (especially orthodox Chakravanti) recite entire texts during important rituals. Time-consuming as this may be, it's considered a potent exercise of willpower, devotion and spiritual purity. </span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Do you people have any suggestions on how I could portrait a Chakravanti of the like? How could I adapt him to this religion, and if by doing this, he could still maintain his duty as one of The Wheel? What foci one could possibly use, as well as practices? <br /> <br /> Thanks in advance - have a great one!</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13197-skeeper0","name":"Skeeper0","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-18T14:06:43-08:00","id":1275162,"title":"","content":"I think you are misunderstanding Orthodox in that sentence. It means strict traditionalist not a member of a branch of a religion called Orthodox","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-18T14:31:26-08:00","id":1275166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1275149-christian-orthodox-euthanatoi?p=1275162#post1275162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you are misunderstanding Orthodox in that sentence. It means strict traditionalist not a member of a branch of a religion called Orthodox</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I know, I know, but I put &quot;Orthodox&quot; in the current situation, that of being a Christian, since that is where the action will happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13197-skeeper0","name":"Skeeper0","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-18T16:20:43-08:00","id":1275198,"title":"","content":"Well, if you want an Eastern Orthodox Christian Euthanatos? You want to make a member of the Knights of Radamanthys. While not Christian as an organization, they modeled themselves after Christian knightly orders to disguise themselves, and pull heavily from people from the areas of the world where Eastern Orthodox Christianity is more common.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-19T04:29:52-08:00","id":1275263,"title":"","content":"I think it's pretty much impossible to create a &quot;Christian&quot; euthanatos. He could hail from a Christian country, but Euthanatos ideology is pure antithesis to Christian doctrine. There are reasons if most traditions find the Euthanatos &quot;creepy&quot; and there are reasons if among them the Celestial Chorus Is One of the most overtly hostile to the Euthanatos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-19T05:49:04-08:00","id":1275274,"title":"","content":"To clarify something, are you asking about Eastern Orthodox Euthanatos or Eastern Orthodox Chakravanti? There were other organizations than the Chakravanti that were incorporated back into the Tradition back when it was formed, not all of which believed in a cycle on reincarnation. It is entirely possible that there were groups of Christian mages with enough of a death fixation that they found a place in the Euthanatoi.<br /> <br /> However, if you are looking for an Eastern Orthodox Chakravanti, one who uses the tools and practices of the Chakravanti while maintaining Eastern Orthodox beliefs and traditions... well I'm not sure you can do that and realistically call the Mage either Eastern Orthodox or Chakravanti. Instead you would have a Mage with a syncretic belief system who merges both philosophies into something different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-19T05:54:01-08:00","id":1275276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1275149-christian-orthodox-euthanatoi?p=1275198#post1275198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, if you want an Eastern Orthodox Christian Euthanatos? You want to make a member of the Knights of Radamanthys. While not Christian as an organization, they modeled themselves after Christian knightly orders to disguise themselves, and pull heavily from people from the areas of the world where Eastern Orthodox Christianity is more common.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. 100%","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-19T09:08:45-08:00","id":1275308,"title":"","content":"While running 100% pure Christian as a Euthanatos is hard, having someone that mixes really isn't. There's a lot of smaller factions that do things differently from the Charkavanti basis of Tradition but manage to make it work. Once you get past the specific interpretation of fate/predestination that the Hindu based &quot;common&quot; style of the Tradition is based on, you can find a lot of ways to meld the Traditions beliefs with beliefs of groups you might not expect.<br /> <br /> Consider a mage that believes that everyone has a predestined divine purpose, but Satan is constantly trying to tempt them off their path to damnation. Mages exist to have the power of intercession like the prophets and saints of old, to fight demonic influence and keep humanity on a just and righteous trajectory.<br /> <br /> Chorister? Easily. But that works into the Euthanatos just fine as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-19T09:50:39-08:00","id":1275314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1275149-christian-orthodox-euthanatoi?p=1275308#post1275308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While running 100% pure Christian as a Euthanatos is hard, having someone that mixes really isn't. There's a lot of smaller factions that do things differently from the Charkavanti basis of Tradition but manage to make it work. Once you get past the specific interpretation of fate/predestination that the Hindu based &quot;common&quot; style of the Tradition is based on, you can find a lot of ways to meld the Traditions beliefs with beliefs of groups you might not expect.<br /> <br /> Consider a mage that believes that everyone has a predestined divine purpose, but Satan is constantly trying to tempt them off their path to damnation. Mages exist to have the power of intercession like the prophets and saints of old, to fight demonic influence and keep humanity on a just and righteous trajectory.<br /> <br /> Chorister? Easily. But that works into the Euthanatos just fine as well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's actually a great idea, and thank you all for helping me and coming with suggestions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13197-skeeper0","name":"Skeeper0","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-19T10:29:54-08:00","id":1275322,"title":"","content":"You can arrive at a Christian acceptance of the Chodona by way of Origen, as long as you're more radical about categorical movement of souls than he was. (Origen <i>probably </i>did not believe that a soul would re-incarnate in a human body, though it appears possible to graduate upwards into a saintly or intercessionary role, becoming akin to an angel.)<br /> <br /> Something like &quot;All intelligences began united in the presence of God, and have withdrawn from Him in proportion to the degree that their ardor for Him cooled. The fire of divinity cannot be extinguished, however, and each soul will be marked by the heat it has deferred, either regaining it through contemplation and affection for the divine, or through self-made punishment after death. It is our duty to shepherd this process, encouraging souls to turn to the light, and releasing tainted intelligences to endure their punishment before they, through their impious conduct, pile further harm upon themselves.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Knights are a good place to start in terms of foci and such. Saintly icons, relics, and meditations. Self-deprivation and asceticism. Fervent prayer.<br /> <br /> (These are the Chodona requirements)<br /> <br /> 1.) Belief in incarnation and/or metempsychosis.<br /> 2.) Belief that souls are eternal, and born of one source, regardless of their current state.<br /> 3.) Accept the role of death and decay in the process of the journey of souls and their eventual return to their source.<br /> 4.) Acceptance of a duty to preserve this system, and to protect humankind and the world, so that the cosmic cycle can complete its work.<br /> 5.) Seek spiritual betterment and ritual purity. Eschew worldly desires.<br /> 6.) Empathy for the suffering of others.<br /> 7.) Eschew actions for one's own desires in favor of higher, spiritual duty.<br /> 8.) Initiates must understand death to protect the cycle; all initiates must undergo a death-like experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-19T17:39:33-08:00","id":1275410,"title":"","content":"One thing to consider is that, from a Christian perspective, any member of the Traditions is, technically, a heretic, with even the Celestial Chorus essentially using Christianity as a &quot;gateway art&quot; (to borrow a term from the Akashic Brotherhood) to their own gnostic belief system. In the terms of the European Thanatoics - the Greek, Irish and even Nordic ones - this actually works out fairly well. The Pomegranate Deme are already a mystery cult, so they could easily hide themselves behind an Orthodox Christian sect, with appropriate Saints and Angels being masks for Hellenic dieties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}